==============================================================================
INTERPRETATION
==============================================================================
EEG identity accuracy            : 0.7813
best non-EEG modality            : 0.9728
chance                           : 0.0500

Participant identity is recoverable from non-EEG channels at
many times chance, including channels carrying no cognitive
content. Fingerprinting is a property of repeated within-person
recording, not of electroencephalography. Window-level
partitioning is therefore unsafe for any biosignal modality,
ECG included, and the scope of this paper's finding is wider
than EEG.

